WEBVTT

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:04.480
<i>It's spring.</i>

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:09.650
<i>And practically a year to 
the day since I joined Eagle Jump.</i>

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.250
<i>I'm well and used to the company by now.</i>

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:20.130
Hi, I'm Suzukaze Aoba. 
Feel free to ask me for help.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:23.120
Hi, I'm Suzukaze Aoba. 
Feel free to ask me for help.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.960
<i>And now, it's my turn to take 
a fresh batch of new hires under my wing!</i>

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.300
Good morning. Something on your mind?

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.970
Toyama-san! Good morning!

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:38.000
It's just, the thought of being a role model 
for the new hires gave me butterflies.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.560
But we're not hiring anybody new this year.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:45.060
Huh?

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.170
What?!

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:52.030
I'm sorry. We're just not that big a company.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:55.810
Of all the embarrassing things 
to be caught doing...

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:58.370
Don't worry. I won't tell anyone.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:00.760
Oh. Can I get you something to drink?

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.300
That would be great, thanks.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:07.050
May I have some coffee? 
With milk and sugar, please.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:08.960
Got it.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:17.380
Yagami-san? Did you stay the night?

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:23.270
Morning...

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:27.020
I had something I wanted to finish up.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:31.890
I seem to recall a similar situation 
exactly one year ago.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.860
A year ago?

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.200
Right... I guess it's April already.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:43.200
<i>I've gotten desensitized to 
seeing Yagami-san in her underwear!</i>

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.430
What's wrong?

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.960
C-Could you please put something on already?

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.230
Huh? You weren't complaining a second ago!

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:51.730
Good morning. 
Want some too, Ko-chan?

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:53.750
Sure, thanks!

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.800
Aoba, you taking your coffee black?

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:00.760
Huh? Well, no.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:04.150
Black coffee tastes bad, 
so mine has milk and sugar.

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:07.160
Oh? So you <i>have</i> matured a bit.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:11.150
Good morning!

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.590
Oh, good morning.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:17.050
Today's the day the new hires arrive, right?

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:19.970
Gotta make sure I keep my cool this year!

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:20.780
Huh?

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:24.410
Hi, I'm Shinoda Hajime. 
If you need anything, just ask!

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:28.580
Oh, please, call me Hajime-san.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:30.450
Or something like that.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.970
Hajime-san, were you watching me earlier?

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:34.370
Huh? Watching what?

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:36.800
Mornin'.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.990
Morning, Yun.

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:41.300
What's this I hear? New hires?

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:44.940
Yeah. Just making sure we 
don't let our nerves get to us.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.140
Um, actually...

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.390
N-New people?

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:52.660
Oh, good morning, Hifumi-senpai.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:54.830
What if they're awful?

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:57.590
I-I-I don't know what I'd do!

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:01.210
It's okay! We're not actually 
taking anyone this year.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:04.740
Shucks. Just Hajime jumpin' the gun, huh?

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:08.040
I'm torn between disappointment and relief.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:12.800
Meanin' Aoba-chan's still 
the youngest and newest here.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.290
No kidding.

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:18.370
Ko-chan, don't you think you 
should get dressed already?

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:20.920
Oh, shoot! I totally forgot.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.790
Didja stay the night again, Yagami-san?

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:27.220
We're not even that busy right now.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:30.430
All we're doing is helping out other teams.

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:33.850
I wanted to reach a good stopping point.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:38.500
It's best to get what we can out of 
the way before our next project starts.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:42.030
When d'you think they'll 
figure out our next project?

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:45.280
Hazuki-san's running late with her part.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:46.580
Upsy-daisy.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:48.340
Say, Mozuku-chan.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:52.080
Any idea what kind of game 
your owner has in mind?

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:57.150
Has anyone here seen Hazuki-san?

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:59.260
Good morning, Umiko-san.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:04.700
Hazuki-san should be here already. 
Especially seeing as Mozuku-chan is here.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.130
Well, this is a problem.

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:10.850
I wanted her feedback on 
the new prototype as soon as possible.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.270
What's the rush?

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:15.670
We'll be busy enough once the project starts.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:18.400
Now's our chance to kick back 
and have some fun.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.340
I could say the same to you.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:22.900
I see you stayed overnight working again.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:27.990
Incidentally, I also had an all-nighter 
recently, playing airsoft in the mountains.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:29.910
B-Bundle of energy, aren't you?

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:34.120
I hear ya, though. I'm down to have 
some fun before it gets busy again.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.580
It ain't like you need an excuse.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.380
But, wow...

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:41.500
Our new game is just around the corner!

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.360
Aoba, hold still.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:55.260
What say we have a cherry 
blossom viewing tomorrow?

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.980
<b>Cherry Blossom Viewing Tomorrow!!</b>

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:57.980
This isn't good.

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:02.320
One last push and I'll be done,
but I'm just not feeling it,

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.250
so I've barely made any...

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:11.620
<i>T-Takimoto-kun is smiling! S-So cute!</i>

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:14.270
Ahem. Quite the lively talk, here.

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:15.820
Ah, Hazuki-san.

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:17.300
Good morning.

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:19.380
So what's this discussion about?

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:24.010
Hajime-san suggested we experiment 
with models that are easier to animate.

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:28.770
Hifumi-senpai was coming up with all 
these ideas like you wouldn't believe!

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:33.080
It was... nothing special...

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:37.810
I'm sorry. I couldn't help it, 
you were so cute.

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:42.970
It's just, you've gotten so much 
more expressive, Takimoto-kun.

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:44.570
I think that's great.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:46.170
Thank you...

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:49.820
By the way, we were talking about it earlier,

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:53.830
but what's the new game 
shaping up to be like?

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:58.150
I've had Umiko-kun working on 
a prototype based on preliminary specs

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:01.880
so we could try out some ideas, 
but it's been difficult.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:03.210
I see.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:07.180
Really, if any of you can bring 
in a good enough proposal,

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:08.930
it could very well be accepted.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.660
Huh? Really?

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:13.220
Then I vote we do a hero team!

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:16.320
Though a magical girl game is tempting, too.

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:17.570
Is that all ya think about?

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:18.970
What about you, Yun?

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:21.820
I reckon somethin' more serious sounds good.

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:24.580
I think I'd still go with fantasy.

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:27.570
When anything's on the table, 
it can be hard to decide.

00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:29.180
And you, Takimoto-kun?

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:29.780
Huh?!

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:31.310
I...

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:35.160
agree with Aoba-chan...

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:40.420
Do you? Stick to what we know 
and keep doing fantasy, then?

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:43.740
Oh, yeah! We're going cherry 
blossom viewing tomorrow.

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:48.770
We're invitin' some other teams, too. 
'Course, you're also welcome, Hazuki-san.

00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:52.010
I'd be happy to join in.
I'll even bring some goodies.

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:53.800
Yay!

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:53.800
Goodies!

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:01.400
Target acquired!

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:04.150
Now, how should I surprise her?

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:08.780
She spotted me?!

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:14.420
I-It couldn't be! 
Not at this distance, for sure....

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:16.100
Must have been a coincidence.

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:17.950
Huh? She's gone.

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:21.100
Hello?

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:22.080
<i>Found you.</i>

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:27.200
<i>Such a novice mistake, 
taking your eyes off your target.</i>

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:29.510
Wh-Where are you?!

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:31.130
<i>Behind you.</i>

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:34.640
Bang.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:36.260
Wrong side.

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:38.520
Come on!

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:42.690
Mmm, yummy...

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:44.650
I see you haven't changed.

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:47.770
That red bean sundae looks good, too!

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:49.020
Would you like some?

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:50.120
Can I?!

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:53.110
Okay, ah!

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:56.990
<i>Well, I'll just think of it 
like feeding an animal.</i>

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:02.910
Mmm, yum...

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:05.070
Okay, your turn!

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:07.880
I'm fine, thank you.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:11.010
Huh? Don't tell me you're embarrassed?

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:13.450
I most certainly am not.

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:15.270
Really?

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.510
All right, fine. I'll have some.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:21.020
Then say, "Ah!"

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:23.830
Too slow! Yoink!

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:28.190
I was just kidding! I didn't mean it, okay?

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:35.570
So, what is it that you wanted my help with?

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:39.860
I'm afraid I won't be of much help 
if it's about your college studies.

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:41.510
It's not that.

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:46.330
Um, promise you won't laugh?

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:48.270
I might, depending.

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:50.090
You meanie!

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:51.840
<b>Single Player
Two Player
Quit</b>

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:51.840
A game?

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:53.990
You made this?

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:56.800
Yep! Ain't it something?

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:56.800
<b>Single Player
Two Players
Quit</b>

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:00.690
Well, the art is sure something.

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:04.180
Cut me some slack! I can't draw.

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:07.130
But it actually runs and everything, see?

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:10.310
You can jump and even attack.

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:13.240
It crashed again!

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:16.680
I take it you want help with programming,

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:18.780
which is why you called me.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:22.290
Before, I couldn't even get it to start.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:26.090
But once it gets going, it seems to work fine.

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:28.950
Come over here, and let me have a look.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:33.420
Sure thing!

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:37.800
Right here. Do you see it?

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:41.030
It was calling the same 
operation over and over again!

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:43.450
I see. Spotted like a true pro!

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:46.850
Do you enjoy programming?

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:51.130
I dunno. It's pretty hard.

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:54.990
But I think I sort of understand 
how Aocchi feels now.

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:56.610
It's not the same as drawing,

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:59.740
but it's neat watching your 
creation come together.

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:05.000
Plus, now I kinda get how programmers feel
when they pray that nobody finds any bugs.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.500
You never considered that while debugging?

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:12.870
Though, if anything, it's more worrying 
when none are found at all.

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:14.880
Oh? Really?

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:17.260
It's only natural to have bugs.

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:21.140
Fixing them and improving the product 
are all part of the workflow.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:24.510
Having none at all is irregular.

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:27.900
I see. So it's okay to have bugs.

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:29.900
That makes me feel better.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:33.940
Of course, a bug this elementary 
speaks to your skill level.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:35.900
Yeah, I know!

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:39.340
Anyway, show me again once 
you've made some more progress.

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:45.030
Does this mean I have potential?

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:47.160
You take things far too positively.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:53.440
Oh, and don't tell Aocchi. 
At least not until I finish this game.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:54.600
Yes, all right.

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:01.760
I used to be... too tense 
to show my feelings...

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:05.680
but I did my best to change... 
and people saw that,

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.130
Sojiro.

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:16.680
And you, Takimoto-kun?

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:17.480
Huh?!

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:19.370
I...

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:22.990
agree with Aoba-chan...

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:28.570
But... I couldn't bring myself...
to voice my own opinion.

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:33.460
I have to stop... making that face!

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:42.380
My thoughts on the last 
project's development?

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:43.480
That's right.

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:48.350
Every April, we ask employees for feedback 
regarding their work over the past year.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:53.200
What went well, what could have gone better, 
or even your goals for the future.

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:54.730
Anything you want to say?

00:11:54.730 --> 00:12:00.910
U-Um... Will anything I say here negatively 
impact my performance report?

00:12:00.910 --> 00:12:03.420
N-No, of course not!

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:04.920
Then...

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:08.450
Why is our team only women?

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:11.980
So you've caught on.

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:14.810
Still, don't you think it's better this way?

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:17.250
S-So it's all a matter of your preferences?

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:21.230
Not at all! Our hiring practices are 
based on skill and personality!

00:12:21.230 --> 00:12:23.160
The team happened to end up all female!

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:25.760
You and your silly jokes, Hazuki-san!

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:30.150
Ah, but say we let men in, 
and one of them snatches Yagami from you.

00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:32.430
Could you live with that, Toyama-kun?

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:34.810
We're not talking about me right now!

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:38.270
Do you have any other thoughts, Suzukaze-kun?

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:40.880
Yes. Um...

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:45.030
It was a privilege to help out under 
my role model, Yagami-san.

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:49.200
I couldn't have asked for more 
from this past year.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:52.320
I only hope I'll be able 
to contribute even more

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:56.470
and create all sorts of characters, 
not just villagers.

00:12:56.470 --> 00:12:57.820
I see.

00:12:57.820 --> 00:13:00.880
Although, you <i>can</i> be greedier, you know.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:04.730
Greedier? You mean about my salary?

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:07.010
Well, that's important, too.

00:13:07.610 --> 00:13:08.800
Things to improve on?

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:13.600
Personally, I think everything 
went pretty well this time around.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:17.900
The two of you had great chemistry 
and made for a good team.

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:20.860
That's for sure. 
Rin was always there to save my neck.

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:25.710
But there's no telling when 
our relationship might change.

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:26.490
Huh?

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:27.690
Ko-chan!

00:13:27.690 --> 00:13:31.510
I-If you ever find someone you want 
to marry, please be honest with me!

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:33.650
That's just how life goes, I know!

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:34.510
Huh?

00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:37.750
Looks like the no-men policy stays.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.790
My... goals?

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:42.370
Um...

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:47.230
Uh...

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:53.470
I... want to overcome... my social anxiety...

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:55.410
Attagirl! You show 'em!

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:57.190
Please take this seriously.

00:13:58.550 --> 00:13:59.940
U-Um...

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:05.790
Yesterday... I said I wanted 
the same genre as Aoba-chan...

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:11.680
but I'd actually prefer 
a more modern setting...

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:15.430
or maybe... a stylish sort of world...

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:17.460
That's... all...

00:14:18.980 --> 00:14:20.810
Oh goodness, I'm sorry.

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:23.300
Relax. I was just surprised.

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:26.240
Good on you for telling me. Thank you.

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:28.050
We'll take it into consideration.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:30.500
R-Right...

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:34.430
Could you save that for after the meeting?

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:39.080
Ah, yes. Takimoto-kun, any interest 
in being character team leader?

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:45.420
For the next project, Toyama-kun's moving up
to producer and Yagami-kun to art director.

00:14:45.420 --> 00:14:49.990
So we're looking for someone else 
to lead the character team.

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:53.060
N-No one's forcing you, don't worry.

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:58.250
I think she was too shocked 
to absorb any of that.

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:00.750
Myself, the lead programmer?

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:04.420
That seems like the sensible assignment.

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:09.550
If only you could give Takimoto-kun 
half the self-assurance you have.

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:11.290
I'm not sure how I'd do that,

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:13.980
but I'll take the role of lead 
under one condition.

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:14.890
What's that?

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:18.220
Each time you change the specs, 
I get to punish you....

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:19.390
with a forehead flick.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:22.180
B-But we can't <i>not</i> update the specs!

00:15:22.180 --> 00:15:23.860
Would you rather release a bad game?

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:25.380
I am well aware of that.

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:28.700
I simply want you to make 
changes responsibly.

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:35.490
You're always waltzing into our cubicles, 
gleefully announcing, "New design specs!"

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:39.620
But have you considered how we feel,
knowing we'll have to rewrite our code?

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:42.370
Knowing it's another night at the office?

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:46.190
Who knew that under that stern face

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:50.260
you were so sweet and caring toward your teammates, Umiko-chan?

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:52.760
Would you prefer this?

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:54.820
I'll take the forehead flick!

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:57.550
I'll be overseeing the project too, this time,

00:15:57.550 --> 00:16:00.640
so I won't let things get too out of hand.

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:05.110
And as far as I'm concerned, being flicked 
on the forehead by a girl is a reward!

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:07.240
Even if it's from you, Umiko-kun.

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:13.010
Then we have an agreement.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:19.140
<i>I, Hazuki Shizuku, had no idea then
that I would come to rue the day</i>

00:16:19.140 --> 00:16:23.210
<i>that I blithely agreed 
to have my forehead flicked.</i>

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:25.580
I've brought a game proposal!

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:26.740
A proposal?

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:29.340
<b>Go To Five</b>

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:29.340
Game Proposal

00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:29.340
Oh, it came up in our discussion yesterday.

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:32.870
But I didn't expect anyone 
to complete one overnight.

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:40.560
I'm afraid this won't cut it.

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:42.190
Figures...

00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:44.100
Do you know why this won't work?

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:47.440
Well, I knew we'd never
do a hero team project.

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:48.940
I just couldn't let it go.

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:51.380
Yes, you're right.

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:55.780
But this proposal 
clearly shows your passion.

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:58.410
That part is very important.

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:01.310
What's your target demographic?

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:04.470
I imagined it as being for kids,

00:17:04.470 --> 00:17:09.210
but I guess the battle system 
is more for older players.

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:12.360
So you're saying I should 
focus on one audience!

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:14.590
Right. That would help.

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:16.700
Can I bring this to you again?

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:21.490
Of course. I personally thought 
the battle system was well done,

00:17:21.490 --> 00:17:23.310
so I'd like you to expand on that.

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:25.060
You got it!

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:31.110
You know we can't accept 
every proposal that's good.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:33.940
I'll make sure she doesn't disrupt anything.

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:38.320
Well, I got twin younger siblings, 
a brother and sister.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:42.200
Hearin' them say the game was fun 
sure put a smile on my heart.

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:44.450
I'm glad to hear that.

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:50.170
Also, I'm mighty awed by how 
both Aoba-chan and Hajime have goals

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.300
and interests they're pursuin'.

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:53.800
Meanwhile...

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:57.020
here I more or less happened upon this job,

00:17:57.020 --> 00:17:59.300
so I ain't so sure I belong.

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:01.300
Do you dislike your current position?

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:02.780
Oh, no, that ain't it!

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:06.680
I'm still learnin', but I like 
animals and monsters, so it's fun.

00:18:07.220 --> 00:18:11.790
None of us have a bad word to say 
about your work or passion.

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:15.030
So I really think you 
shouldn't sell yourself short.

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:19.180
I know it can be difficult to figure out 
what you want to do,

00:18:19.180 --> 00:18:22.530
but I hope you'll at least 
stay with us until then.

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:26.500
You're as valuable a member of 
the team as anyone.

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:27.740
Right...

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:30.920
And that does it.

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:32.740
Yes, that's everyone.

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:35.420
They were all so cute.

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:37.860
They've grown into quite the fine team,

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:39.180
don't you think?

00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:40.850
Yes, of course.

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:44.930
And this cute team of yours is 
waiting for the new project to begin.

00:18:44.930 --> 00:18:48.600
Right. Well, I'm in a good 
mood to be productive.

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:52.190
So, the cherry blossom viewing's tonight.

00:18:52.530 --> 00:18:55.030
I wonder what I should bring.

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:57.580
<i>You'll</i> be staying till 
you finish your work.

00:18:57.580 --> 00:18:58.820
A shame, I know.

00:18:58.820 --> 00:18:59.910
You're kidding!

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:06.790
I made us some food.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:09.110
Please, help yourselves.

00:19:09.110 --> 00:19:10.920
Wow, it looks delicious!

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:13.290
I bought some sushi.

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:17.070
I didn't have the chance 
to cook like Toyama-kun.

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:19.050
Wow! Talk about a treat!

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:22.050
I just brought some sweets.

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:26.350
I brought... some sake...

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:28.100
Cheers!

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:31.040
So good!

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:37.650
Mmm, so good! Your cooking is the best, Rin!

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:46.120
Say that one more time.

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:47.350
Huh? Why?

00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:48.530
Just because!

00:19:48.530 --> 00:19:51.000
Ooh, this looks good, too!

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:51.580
Huh?

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:53.630
That fatty tuna is mine!

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:57.960
Hey! There aren't enough for everyone!

00:19:58.820 --> 00:20:00.290
You snooze, you lose.

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:01.970
Fine! Then the sea urchin's mine!

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:05.800
And one for you, Aoba. 
For your one-year anniversary.

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:07.850
Huh? For me?

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:12.100
<i>Oh, no... Wasabi. Now what?</i>

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:14.750
Whoops. Can't handle wasabi?

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:17.530
N-No, I can handle it just fine!

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:18.980
Oh, really?

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:21.240
This is nothing!

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:28.870
Aoba-chan, it ain't no shame to admit it.

00:20:29.310 --> 00:20:30.870
Hazuki-san,

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:34.870
I trust you haven't forgotten 
our little conversation.

00:20:34.870 --> 00:20:39.070
Remember... Each time you change the specs...

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:39.880
Bang.

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:42.470
A flick! We agreed to a forehead flick!

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:44.970
Here's version two of my proposal!

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:44.970
<b>Go To Five</b>

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:48.370
I took the battle concept to the next level!

00:20:48.370 --> 00:20:50.180
Huh? You revised it already?

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:56.270
Now both the hero and villain teams have 
five members—so everyone has a rival!

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:59.290
It'll be double the fun!

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:02.900
Okay, great, just try not 
to get ahead of yourself.

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:08.510
All right! Attention, please!

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:13.540
I know everyone's having fun, 
but it's about time we wrapped it up.

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:17.710
I'd like to close with a 
very important announcement.

00:21:18.070 --> 00:21:19.680
An important announcement?

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:21.090
I wonder what it is.

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:24.730
Our next project's specifications 
are just about finalized.

00:21:24.730 --> 00:21:29.090
As such, we're planning to hold 
another character design competition.

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:34.020
Let your imaginations flow free, 
and present your own visions

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:37.170
of characters that fit the design specs.

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:40.190
Huh? So whoever's designs are chosen...

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:44.030
They will, of course, become 
the project's character designer.

00:21:44.380 --> 00:21:48.080
A-And I'm allowed to participate too, right?

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:49.370
Why wouldn't you be?

00:21:49.750 --> 00:21:52.850
Ko-chan entered right after 
joining the company,

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:56.500
and her designs ended up being 
chosen for <i>Fairies Story</i>.

00:22:03.710 --> 00:22:06.470
Th-Then I'll give it a shot, too!

00:22:07.130 --> 00:22:09.970
I'll put forth everything I have!

00:22:13.350 --> 00:22:16.600
I expect great things, Suzukaze-kun.

00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:17.770
Right!

00:22:18.350 --> 00:22:20.720
<i>The whole reason I joined this company</i>

00:22:20.720 --> 00:22:24.490
<i>was that I wanted to become a 
character designer like Yagami-san.</i>

00:22:27.230 --> 00:22:29.820
<i>So I'm not gonna pass up any opportunity.</i>

00:22:30.500 --> 00:22:33.240
<i>This is my dream, after all!</i>
